Hi,
For coding allele D in Y chromosome,

Case 1.
Grand Mother  a(150) b(150)
Grand Father   c(146) d(=Y,156?)
           Mother a(150) b(150)
           Father  a(150) c(146)
Should I code this as, ab X ac. Since, D allele is not coming in F1.

Case 2.
Grand Mother   (119)   (119)
Grand Father    (107)  (=Y, 119?))
           Mother  (119)  (119)
           Father   (119)  (107)
(119)(119) = AC/BC = 7; (119)(107) = AD/BD= 8; How should allele "D" be assigned in the "Y" chromosome?

Case 3.
Grand Mother   (146)   (156)
Grand Father    (122)  (=Y, 132?))
           Mother  (132)  (156)
           Father   (132)  (146)
(132)(132) = not AC = 11; (132)(156) = not BC= 12; (132)(146) = not AD= 13;  (146)(156) = BD=4 ??

Best regards,
Mehedi

